<title>USA: CME appoints two new outside directors.</title>
<headline>CME appoints two new outside directors.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-03-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Chicago Mercantile Exchange said its board of directors named two new directors on Wednesday, completing its 1997 appointments.</p>
<p>The new directors are David Puth, managing director in Chase Manhattan Bank's forex derivatives group, and Verne Sedlacek, executive vice president and chief financial officer of Harvard Management Co, a subsidiary of Harvard University.</p>
<p>&quot;The knowledge and expertise that David Puth and Verne Sedlacek bring to the table will round out our board as we face a new century,&quot; CME chairman Jack Sandner said in a statement.</p>
<p>((Chicago Derivatives Desk 312-408-8750))</p>
<p>((E-mail: derivatives@reuters.com))</p>
